---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { CANON_PATHS, LINKS, linkClass } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const ext = { target: "_blank", rel: "noopener noreferrer" };

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "Is this a product review?",
    a: "No. It is how to read the field. The two models are on GunSearchEngine. The three numbers stay apart at FFLIntel.",
  },
  {
    q: "What is the fog of sell-through?",
    a: "Treating last month’s closed units as if they were the map of what people are trying to find now. What rang is an after-action report. The scout is the ask.",
  },
  {
    q: "Where should I go next?",
    a: "GunSearchEngine if you want the models. Demand Intelligence if you buy the category. GunSearchAgent if you run a site. FFLIntel if you need the three numbers kept apart.",
  },
] as const;

const doors = [
  {
    href: LINKS.fortress,
    label: "Sell-through and search — GunSearchEngine",
  },
  {
    href: LINKS.demandIntel,
    label: "Demand Intelligence",
  },
  {
    href: LINKS.gsa,
    label: "GunSearchAgent",
  },
  {
    href: LINKS.fflintel,
    label: "FFLIntel",
  },
] as const;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="The Fog of Sell-Through — Art of Demand | Betsy Tzu"
  description="Last month’s sell-through is last season’s map. Reads the register. Does not confuse it with what people are trying to find now."
  path="/art-of-demand-retailbi"
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.tzu}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <p
      class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3"
    >
      Betsy Tzu · Art of Demand
    </p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white mb-4">
      Know the terrain before the register rings
    </h1>
    <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400 mb-6">
      Last month’s sell-through is last season’s map. A good operator still
      reads it. A wise one does not march as if the river has not moved.
    </p>
    <figure class="mb-8">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.tzu)}
        alt="Betsy Tzu — The Art of Demand"
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full rounded-2xl object-cover ring-1 ring-zinc-700/80"
      />
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-center text-xs text-zinc-600">
        Betsy Tzu — preparation over theater
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">
      <p>
        In this trade the choice is the order, the floor set, the page you put
        up before Saturday. What already rang is true. It is also late. It tells
        you where the army camped. It does not tell you where the next column is
        walking.
      </p>
      <p>
        Call that delay the <strong class="text-zinc-200">fog of sell-through</strong
        >. A monthly same-store print is an after-action report: an honest count
        of what sold. Useful. Incomplete. The scout is the ask — the caliber,
        the load, the model someone typed when nothing on the shelf answered
        back. A missed search never becomes a unit. It still happened.
      </p>
      <p>
        Three numbers keep getting folded into one headline. Background checks
        are weather: public, lagged, not sales. The Index is the after-action:
        what a reporting panel actually sold. The ask is the ground underfoot,
        including ground nobody rang up. Collapse them and you plan from a myth.
        Keep them apart and you can still use each one.
      </p>
      <p>
        Supreme excellence is not shouting at last month’s percent-change. It is
        knowing the field while the shopper is still hunting. The dealer who
        reads the ask on their own site is not guessing the next case. The brand
        that reads anonymized search is not waiting for a closed month to learn
        the river moved.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you run a shop,{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchAgent</a> sits
        on your site and writes the asks down. If you buy the category,{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.demandIntel} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >Demand Intelligence</a
        >{" "}
        is that same search across the network. The comparison of the two models
        is on{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchEngine</a>.
        The desk that keeps the three numbers apart is{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fflintel} class={linkClass} {...ext}>FFLIntel</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10 grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
      {
        doors.map((door) => (
          <a
            href={door.href}
            {...ext}
            class="rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800 bg-zinc-950/50 p-5 hover:border-sky-500/40"
          >
            <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">{door.label}</p>
          </a>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-lg font-semibold text-white mb-4">FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="space-y-5">
        {
          faqs.map((item) => (
            <div>
              <dt class="text-sm font-semibold text-zinc-100">{item.q}</dt>
              <dd class="mt-1 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-400">{item.a}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>
    </section>

    <p class="mt-10 text-xs leading-relaxed text-zinc-600">
      Not affiliated with Gearfire or RetailBI. Not 4473 software. Not a
      register.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
